        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Miserere nobis domine miserere nobis et kariatis dulcedine corde nostra perfunde. Quo pacis tue semper conexione firmati. antiqui hostis in cordibus nostris aditus non pateat introeundi. sed sic semper protectionis tuae uelamine tueamur. ut ubique angelorum tuorum excubiis muniarum. Ut si fessa membra quieberint. spiritus tibi uigilet semper. Vigilate tua custodia deus noster qui uiuis.",
          "english": "Have mercy on us, O Lord, have mercy on us, and fill our hearts with the sweetness of [the printed “kariatis” is irregular]. So that, always strengthened by the bond of Thy peace, no entrance into our hearts may lie open to the ancient enemy. But may we always be sheltered by the covering of Thy protection, that everywhere we may be fortified by the watch of Thy angels [the printed “muniarum” is irregular]. So that, if our weary limbs rest [the printed “quieberint” is irregular], our spirit may always keep watch for Thee. [The printed “Vigilate tua custodia” has an unresolved construction], O our God, who livest.",
          "sourcePages": [
            652
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "prepared",
