          "alignment": "reviewed",
          "id": "opening-prayers-b0051",
          "verification": "source-reading-pending",
          "editorialNote": "PDF p.652 visually checked across both columns. Printed “kariatis”, “corde nostra”, “muniarum”, “quieberint” and “Vigilate tua custodia” are irregular. The old prepared English silently normalised these readings; unresolved words are now identified, with earlier English and provenance retained. No different Mozarabic edition is substituted.",
          "originalPreparedEnglish": "Have mercy on us, O Lord, have mercy on us, and fill our hearts with the sweetness of charity, so that, always strengthened by the bond of Thy peace, no entrance into our hearts may lie open to the ancient enemy. May we always be sheltered by the covering of Thy protection, and everywhere fortified by the watch of Thy angels; so that, if our weary limbs rest, our spirit may always keep watch for Thee. May Thy guarding watch keep vigil, O our God, who livest.",
